    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sedan, Montana takes its name from Sedan, Kansas, where John Maddox and his family lived before settling here in 1884.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mtmemory.org/nodes/view/128376"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Leo and Al Meyer opened the Shields Valley Cheese Factory in Sedan in 1914, providing local dairy farmers with a market for their milk.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mtmemory.org/nodes/view/128376"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sedan’s post office opened in 1891 and closed in 1915, reflecting the town’s brief boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mtmemory.org/nodes/view/128376"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1905, 25 residents of Sedan built the East Flathead Telephone Company, stringing lines between homes to stay connected.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mtmemory.org/nodes/view/128376"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "School records and residents’ recollections indicate that over 250 children attended Sedan School throughout the years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
